#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:492
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:494
msgid "No Streaming Unzip API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:496
msgid ""
"Due to the design of the .zip file format, it's impossible to interpret a"
" .zip file from start to finish (such as from a readable stream) without "
"sacrificing correctness. The Central Directory, which is the authority on"
" the contents of the .zip file, is at the end of a .zip file, not the "
"beginning. A streaming API would need to either buffer the entire .zip "
"file to get to the Central Directory before interpreting anything "
"(defeating the purpose of a streaming interface), or rely on the Local "
"File Headers which are interspersed through the .zip file. However, the "
"Local File Headers are explicitly denounced in the spec as being "
"unreliable copies of the Central Directory, so trusting them would be a "
"violation of the spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:504
msgid ""
"Any library that offers a streaming unzip API must make one of the above "
"two compromises, which makes the library either dishonest or "
"nonconformant (usually the latter). This library insists on correctness "
"and adherence to the spec, and so does not offer a streaming API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:508
msgid ""
"Here is a way to create a spec-conformant .zip file using the `zip` "
"command line program (Info-ZIP) available in most unix-like environments,"
" that is (nearly) impossible to parse correctly with a streaming parser:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:516
msgid ""
"This .zip file contains a single file entry that uses General Purpose Bit"
" 3, which means the Local File Header doesn't know the size of the file. "
"Any streaming parser that encounters this situation will either "
"immediately fail, or attempt to search for the Data Descriptor after the "
"file's contents. The file's contents is a sequence of 16-bytes crafted to"
" exactly mimic a valid Data Descriptor for an empty file, which will fool"
" any parser that gets this far into thinking that the file is empty "
"rather than containing 16-bytes. What follows the file's real contents is"
" the file's real Data Descriptor, which will likely cause some kind of "
"signature mismatch error for a streaming parser (if one hasn't occurred "
"already)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:525
msgid ""
"By using General Purpose Bit 3 (and compression method 0), it's possible "
"to create arbitrarily ambiguous .zip files that distract parsers with "
"file contents that contain apparently valid .zip file metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:529
msgid "Limitted ZIP64 Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:531
msgid ""
"For ZIP64, only zip files smaller than `8PiB` are supported, not the full"
" `16EiB` range that a 64-bit integer should be able to index. This is due"
" to the JavaScript Number type being an IEEE 754 double precision float."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:535
msgid "The Node.js `fs` module probably has this same limitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:537
msgid "ZIP64 Extensible Data Sector Is Ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:539
msgid ""
"The spec does not allow zip file creators to put arbitrary data here, but"
" rather reserves its use for PKWARE and mentions something about Z390. "
"This doesn't seem useful to expose in this library, so it is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:543
msgid "No Multi-Disk Archive Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:545
msgid ""
"This library does not support multi-disk zip files. The multi-disk fields"
" in the zipfile spec were intended for a zip file to span multiple floppy"
" disks, which probably never happens now. If the \"number of this disk\" "
"field in the End of Central Directory Record is not `0`, the `open()`, "
"`fromFd()`, `fromBuffer()`, or `fromRandomAccessReader()` `callback` will"
" receive an `err`. By extension the following zip file fields are ignored"
" by this library and not provided to clients:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:552
msgid "Disk where central directory starts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:553
msgid "Number of central directory records on this disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:554
msgid "Disk number where file starts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:556
msgid "Limited Encryption Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:558
msgid ""
"You can detect when a file entry is encrypted with \"Traditional "
"Encryption\" via `isEncrypted()`, but yauzl will not help you decrypt it."
" See `openReadStream()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:562
msgid ""
"If a zip file contains file entries encrypted with \"Strong Encryption\","
" yauzl emits an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:564
msgid "If the central directory is encrypted or compressed, yauzl emits an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:566
msgid "Local File Headers Are Ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:568
msgid ""
"Many unzip libraries mistakenly read the Local File Header data in zip "
"files. This data is officially defined to be redundant with the Central "
"Directory information, and is not to be trusted. Aside from checking the "
"signature, yauzl ignores the content of the Local File Header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:573
msgid "No CRC-32 Checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:575
msgid ""
"This library provides the `crc32` field of `Entry` objects read from the "
"Central Directory. However, this field is not used for anything in this "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:578
msgid "versionNeededToExtract Is Ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:580
msgid ""
"The field `versionNeededToExtract` is ignored, because this library "
"doesn't support the complete zip file spec at any version,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:583
msgid "No Support For Obscure Compression Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:585
msgid ""
"Regarding the `compressionMethod` field of `Entry` objects, only method "
"`0` (stored with no compression) and method `8` (deflated) are supported."
" Any of the other 15 official methods will cause the `openReadStream()` "
"`callback` to receive an `err`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:590
msgid "Data Descriptors Are Ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:592
msgid ""
"There may or may not be Data Descriptor sections in a zip file. This "
"library provides no support for finding or interpreting them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:595
msgid "Archive Extra Data Record Is Ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:597
msgid ""
"There may or may not be an Archive Extra Data Record section in a zip "
"file. This library provides no support for finding or interpreting it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:600
msgid "No Language Encoding Flag Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yauzl_README.md:602
msgid ""
"Zip files officially support charset encodings other than CP437 and "
"UTF-8, but the zip file spec does not specify how it works. This library "
"makes no attempt to interpret the Language Encoding Flag."
msgstr ""

